{"term":"fold","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:320de464a6df35d2b2","definition":"To bend (any thin material, such as paper) over so that it comes in contact with itself.","example":"Next, fold the paper over, so the right half is on top of the left half.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bend","crease"],"antonyms":["unfold"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ad406ef15332a26d2a","definition":"To make the proper arrangement (in a thin material) by bending.","example":"If you fold the sheets, they'll fit more easily in the drawer.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["unfold"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ef589ce3e8d77dd38f","definition":"To draw or coil (one’s arms, a snake’s body, etc.) around something so as to enclose or embrace it.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["unfold"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:beeb4fdac9600e0ce0","definition":"To stir (semisolid ingredients) gently, with an action as if folding over a solid.","example":"Fold the egg whites into the batter.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["unfold"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:09afbea17debb27401","definition":"To become folded; to form folds.","example":"Cardboard doesn't fold very easily.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["unfold"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b689aa95c1729e69a9","definition":"To fall over; to collapse or give way; to be crushed.","example":"The chair folded under his enormous weight.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["buckle","cave","cave in","crumple","fall over"],"antonyms":["unfold"],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal, intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c902cb3ec7e969e6a1","definition":"To give way on a point or in an argument.","example":"He folded that point and didn't bring it up again.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["buckle","cave","cave in","crumple","concede","give in","give way","yield"],"antonyms":["unfold"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8cb206143c6ba76cf7","definition":"To withdraw from betting.","example":"With no hearts in the river and no chance to hit his straight, he folded.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["unfold"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fold#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bb7ca183ed825bd502","definition":"To withdraw or quit in general.","e